# Everything both Dockerfiles must never see. They each do `COPY . .`, so
# without this file the build context carries the live Neon DSN, the AWS keys
# and the Shopify secrets to the daemon and bakes them into a build-stage
# layer - recoverable from the image even though the final stage copies out
# only the compiled binary.

# Secrets - the whole reason this file exists.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
env/

# Git history: large, and carries every secret ever committed.
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Build artefacts and local binaries. createunicornorder.exe alone is ~30MB of
# context that no build stage reads.
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
*.log

# Docs and editor/OS noise.
CLAUDE.md
README.md
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The Dockerfiles themselves - naming them keeps an edit to one from busting
# the other's cached layers.
Dockerfile
*.Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
